00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.630
Christmas and Clara Time.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:44.239
Jenna Coleman did a very general interview
unrelated to Doctor Who but the Special and

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:49.420
her potentially leaving the show came up.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:55.070
She said the Special is all about dreaming,
about what’s real and what’s not.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.340
That’s a very opaque explanation but as
we saw in the teaser Nick Frost as Father

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.090
Christmas or Santa, whatever you want to call
him.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.640
Asking Clara why she stopped believing in
him.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.300
As much as episodes of Doctor Who center on
The Doctor, this feels like it might be a

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.579
story told from Clara’s perspective.

00:01:11.579 --> 00:01:16.729
As if in the course of the adventure they
have, Clara suddenly decides that Father Christmas

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:20.990
is real.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:25.229
That doesn’t mean Nick Frost’s character
is not some advanced alien acting as Father

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:28.509
Christmas, It seems like that’s what’s
really going on.

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:33.779
But Father Christmas and The Doctor share
a lot of the same abilities.

00:01:33.779 --> 00:01:44.909
The ability to travel to everyone’s house
in the span of 

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:46.189
a single night.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:49.280
And containers that are bigger on the inside.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:59.200
When you think about it, isn’t the TARDIS
like a giant bag of gifts.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.399
Not always the gifts you want, but always
the gifts you need.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:06.539
Here’s some background on the scene that
we can use to spin some theories:

00:02:06.539 --> 00:02:08.560
Clara is seen with Father Christmas first
but The TARDIS has already landed behind her.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.560
Even though his sleigh is parked at a weird
angle and there are gifts spilled out all

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.251
over the place I don’t think it crashed.

00:02:14.251 --> 00:02:17.830
It’s implied The Doctor has a pre-existing
relationship with Father Christmas and there

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:21.840
is an urgent matter they are both involved
in that requires Clara.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.570
I don’t think Father Christmas is an evil
character like Missy.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:30.060
So I don’t think The Doctor is trying to
save Clara from imminent demise.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:36.670
He asks her to get her ass in the TARDIS no
questions asked.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:43.400
But based on his interaction with Father Christmas
I think they need her to help solve a problem

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.910
at the North Pole and there’s a ticking
clock.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.130
Time is running out.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:52.640
We know that the episode takes place primarily
at The North Pole at this place and these

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.620
people are the supporting cast.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:03:00.700
This place where they are here is back where
Clara is living now.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.120
The creature in the last trailer looks kind
of like an Ice Warrior without it’s armor

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:13.900
and for a little bit he might be coming after
Nick Frosts people.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:33.120
Like this is they mythological Santa’s Workshop
and this creature is the proverbial Grinch

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.530
trying to ruin Christmas by killing them all.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:47.820
That’s just a fun Doctor Who Doctor Seuss
crossover theory but based on what Jenna Coleman

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:56.990
said in her interview and her conversation
with Nick Frost in the clip.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:00.910
Believing in Father Christmas is a core part
of the solution.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:05.832
So there’s the A story about Clara believing
in made up things that might be totally real

00:04:05.832 --> 00:04:10.680
like Father Christmas or Robin Hood or The
Doctor.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.150
And there’s the B Story - The monster chase
with this creature.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.780
The BBC will continue to post new clips and
promos between now and the special, so fingers

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:22.099
crossed that there’s more new footage that
can explain how the A story and the B story

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:23.099
come together.

00:04:23.099 --> 00:04:26.639
And why Clara is so important to it all.

00:04:26.639 --> 00:04:29.610
Next big question is Clara leaving or not
leaving.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.999
